# What never enters the build context. The image only needs zsh/, packs/ and
# first_boot.sh (see the COPY lines in the Dockerfile); everything else is
# either noise sent to the Docker daemon or user configuration that must not
# be baked into /etc/skel.
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.claude
assets
docs
LICENSE
README.md
scripts
wsl.ps1

# Build artifacts
*.tar
*.vhdx

# A local .env.global is one machine's configuration. COPY zsh would bake it
# into /etc/skel, so every distro, for every user, would inherit it.
# `**/` earns its place: a pattern without a slash only matches at the root of
# the context, while the file this protects - zsh/gmake/.env.global - sits in a
# subdirectory. The two *.sample files are the committed contracts and they
# stay: `**/.env*` would have taken them along.
**/.env
**/.env.global
